WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.133
Q-learning, cell by cell.

2
00:00:02.733 --> 00:00:09.867
Q-learning keeps a table: for every state and action, how good it expects things to be from there.

3
00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:20.100
After every step it nudges one entry toward a target: the reward it just got, plus the best value it currently expects from the next state.

4
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:26.867
It's the running average from week zero again, except the target looks one step into the future.

5
00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:36.533
Reach the exam hall for plus ten. Picking up your phone costs five and ends the episode. Every step costs a little time.

6
00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:50.133
Watch value spread backwards from the exam, one update at a time, until arrows form a path.

7
00:00:50.133 --> 00:01:00.367
Follow the arrows from the start: a shortest path to the exam that avoids both phones. Nobody told it the route. It learned from reward alone.

8
00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:05.200
Next week, the exact same algorithm learns when to quiz a student.

